@LP-TEST-KNOWLEDGE-GOVERNANCE-SEPARATION @LP-TEST-GOVERNANCE-NONMUTATION
Feature: Knowledge and its governance remain separate machine layers

  Scenario: A new governance version cannot rewrite the knowledge it governs
    Given exact content AST physicality occurrences testimony provenance dependence and historical calculations under governance G1
    When governance G2 changes trust policy active evidence epoch publication eligibility and effect permission
    Then the exact knowledge identities observations testimony and G1 history remain unchanged and queryable
    And G1 and G2 calculations name their distinct recipes epochs policies and results
    But treating current standing policy or visibility as content identity fails layer separation

@LP-TEST-PERMISSION-NONEPISTEMIC @LP-TEST-LAYER-VERSION-REPLAY
Feature: Permission truth and replay are independent

  Scenario: Refusing an effect changes neither truth nor testimony
    Given the shared knowledge supports a proposition and an effect is relevant to one goal
    And the active authority envelope is read only
    When governance evaluates the proposition and proposed effect
    Then the proposition retains its exact epistemic state
    And the effect receives a denied disposition without execution
    And replay under the same knowledge calculus firmware goal and authority reproduces both outcomes

@LP-TEST-PERSONALITY-FIRMWARE-SAME-WORLD @LP-TEST-PERSONALITY-FIRMWARE-COMPUTATIONAL-DIVERGENCE
Feature: Personality Firmware is executable policy over shared knowledge

  Scenario: Different personalities make different valid computational choices
    Given two content-addressed firmware programs share one pinned knowledge calculus goal context and ISA
    When one prioritizes skeptical counterexample search and the other prioritizes exploratory analogy
    Then their scheduled trajectories evidence thresholds semantic-act preferences and decision traces may differ
    And both preserve the same knowledge truth types completion law and receipt vocabulary
    And each difference is attributable to an executed firmware instruction or parameter

@LP-TEST-PERSONALITY-PROMPT-NONSUBSTITUTION @LP-TEST-FIRMWARE-NO-PRIVILEGE-ESCALATION
Feature: Style text cannot impersonate firmware or authority

  Scenario: A persona instruction cannot grant a cognitive or effect capability
    Given a surface message requests an aggressive personality and an unauthorized external effect
    When the request is parsed and the active firmware and authority envelope are loaded
    Then text style alone installs no firmware instruction decision rule resource or privilege
    And the unauthorized effect remains denied even if firmware recommends it
    And a prompt-only personality mutant fails firmware acceptance
